<PubmedArticle>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">A higher CRP level was associated with shorter biochemical failure-free survival on univariate and multivariable analyses in patients who received definitive radiation therapy. CRP was also associated with PSA in exploratory subgroups. These findings warrant further exploration in a prospectively enrolled patient cohort.</AbstractText>
